<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "A virtual space is the map view built into every channel. People who are present in the channel can switch from Chat to Space, walk around the shared 8-bit village, and keep using the same public channel conversation."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_control}>{dgettext("help_space", "Opening Space")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "Open any channel and click the Space tab, next to the channel's own tab at the bottom of the chat area. Clicking the channel tab takes you back to the messages. There is no separate invite card or space command for the channel map."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_community}>{dgettext("help_space", "Joining and Moving")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "Entering the channel makes your avatar available in Space. Move with the arrow keys or WASD while the canvas is focused; the server validates every step, so walls and furniture block movement for everyone equally."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_community}>{dgettext("help_space", "Lifecycle")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "Channel spaces are runtime state. They wake when someone views Space, mirror the current channel presence, and can be rebuilt from that presence when the view is opened again."
  )}
</p>
